<title>USA: Ariz. 360 MW Springerville unit seen up end-week.</title>
<headline>Ariz. 360 MW Springerville unit seen up end-week.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The 360 megawatt (MW) unit 1 at the Springerville coal-fired plant in Arizona is not expected to restart until the end of this week, sources familiar with the plant's operations said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The unit was tentatively scheduled to restart Tuesday after being shut in late March for maintenance work.</p>
<p>The Springerville plant is operated by Tucson Electric Power Co.</p>
<p>--Los Angeles bureau + 1 213 955 6761</p>
